{"name":"Bloodstone","hex":"#413431","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bloodstone","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A green chalcedony that is sprinkled with red spots or veins of hematite.","Hematite."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bloodstone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heliotrope (bloodstone)","blocks":[{"text":"Heliotrope, is a mineral aggregate, a cryptocrystalline mixture of quartz that occurs mostly as jasper (opaque) or sometimes as chalcedony (translucent)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Quarz_-_Heliotrop_%28Blutjaspis%29.JPG/330px-Quarz_-_Heliotrop_%28Blutjaspis%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heliotrope_(bloodstone)","wikidata":"Q430174"},{"title":"Bloodstone (1988 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Bloodstone is a 1988 action-adventure film produced by Ashok Amritraj and Sunanda Murali Manohar, directed by Dwight H. Little and written by Nico Mastorakis. Starring Rajinikanth, Brett Stimely and Anna Nicholas, the film was shot primarily in India. The story revolves around a mythical ruby called the \"bloodstone\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d2/Bloodstone_%281988_film%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloodstone_(1988_film)","wikidata":"Q4928017"},{"title":"Bloodstone (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Bloodstone is an American R&B, soul and funk group, most popular in the 1970s and early 1980s. The band charted thirteen songs between 1973 and 1984."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/76/Bloodstone_band%2C_c._1973.jpg/330px-Bloodstone_band%2C_c._1973.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloodstone_(band)","wikidata":"Q2907000"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/co